  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Verizon Business Network Services obligated $407M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Verizon Business Network Services won 376 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.1M. Obligations fell 6.6% year over year. Year-to-year obligations show variability: FY21 recorded $265M, FY22 recorded $496M, FY23 recorded $380M, FY24 recorded $459M, FY25 recorded $436M, and FY26 recorded $407M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $115M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $101M and the Department of Justice at $61.1M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the dominant market, with $353M in obligations, and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) is next at $28.8M. Other notable markets include Telecommunications Resellers at $10.1M and Other Computer Related Services at $1.4M. This profile covers contract obligations only, except where tables list total contract values, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
