          "Verizon Business Network Services saw obligations rise from $265M in FY21 to $496M in FY22, then move to $380M in FY23, $459M in FY24, $436M in FY25, and $407M in FY26.",
          "Verizon Business Network Services has 376 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.1M."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers and which markets matter most?",
        "body": [
          "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $115M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $101M and the Department of Justice at $61.1M.",
          "Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest market at $353M, with Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) at $28.8M and Telecommunications Resellers at $10.1M.",
          "Several smaller markets and agencies round out demand, including the Social Security Administration at $29.6M and the Department of the Treasury at $27.4M."
